+### Font utilities
+
+The font keys ship whole in the utilities layer from the `src/styles/utilities/_font.scss`
+partial: the `.font-monospace` class, the `.fs-1` to `.fs-6` size classes, the `.fst-italic` and
+`.fst-normal` style classes, the `.fw-lighter` to `.fw-bolder` weight classes, and the `.lh-1`,
+`.lh-sm`, `.lh-base`, and `.lh-lg` line-height classes. The release writes none of these entries
+responsive, so each class ships at the empty infix alone and no font class writes a breakpoint
+infix.
+
+A size class resolves what the heading class of the same level resolves: the `.fs-1` class reads
+the `--vn-size-8` token the `.h1` class reads, down to the `.fs-6` class, which reads the
+`--vn-size-3` token the `.h6` class reads. So a retuned size token moves a size class and its
+heading class together, and a size class holds its size at every viewport. The release scales the
+`.fs-1` to `.fs-4` sizes with the viewport and caps them from a 1200px viewport; Veneer writes
+neither the fluid formula nor the cap, as the heading classes write neither.
+
+The `.lh-base` class reads the `--vn-line-body` token the body text reads, so a retuned
+`--vn-line-body` token moves the class with the body text. The `.font-monospace` class reads the
+`--bs-font-monospace` alias, as the release writes it, and the `_tokens.scss` partial declares that
+alias over the `--vn-font-mono-base` token, so a root retune of either name moves the class. The
+weights, the styles, and the other line heights stay literal. A weight class names a point on the
+weight scale, and the `--vn-weight-body` and `--vn-weight-heading` tokens name the weight of a role,
+so a retuned body weight leaves the `.fw-normal` class at 400. No published Veneer token carries a
+style or the other line heights. The `.fw-lighter` and `.fw-bolder` classes resolve against the
+weight their parent resolves, as the release's relative keywords do. No font class reads the
+density factor or the color mode.
+
+The partial writes every entry through the `utility` mixin that § Styles describes, in the
+release's map order: the family, size, style, weight, and line-height entries. No entry sets a
+property another entry sets, so the order that decides a resolution is the order inside an entry:
+an element carrying the `.fw-bold` and `.fw-light` classes resolves the `700` weight, because the
+map writes the bold step after the light step. Every declaration carries the `!important` flag the
+release writes. The classes sit in the utilities layer, so a size class beats a heading or display
+class on the same element: an element carrying the `.h1` and `.fs-6` classes resolves the size the
+`--vn-size-3` token carries. § Styles shows the escape from an important utility inside the
+utilities layer.
+
+The `tests/src/styles/utilities/font.test.ts` proof reads each size class against its heading
+class at the 390 and 1280 viewports and under its retuned size token, the base line height under a
+retuned `--vn-line-body` token, the monospace class under a retuned alias and a retuned token, each
+weight under a 400 and a 600 parent weight, each style inside an oblique parent, each line height
+over a fixed font size, the absence of an infixed class, a dark island and the density factor, the
+order inside an entry, the size class over a heading class, the priority over a later unlayered
+rule, and the escape inside the utilities layer.
+
+These are the keys' recorded departures.
+
+- **The size classes read Veneer's heading scale.** The release writes the `.fs-1` to `.fs-4`
